  "details": "Currently, gestures only really work if they follow the format of being 2 frames long.\n\nYou can make a gesture longer than 2 frames, but it will cause all of your other gestures to break by slowing them down to last as long as whatever gesture you used that was more than 2 frames.\n\nThe current workaround to this problem is to add a disabled gameobject with a separate animator that then animates when disabled. The gesture only needs to toggle the separate gameobject on with its 2 frames, and then the gameobject's animator can last for longer.\n\nWhile this is useful, there are some ways it is used that shouldn't be done this way - such as animating our actual avatar.\n\nI have an avatar with an animation that simply moves a blendshape from 0% to 100% over the course of 5 minutes. To make this work on a gesture, I had throw a duplicate of my avatar onto the main avatar, disable the copy, and put another animator on the copy that does the actual animation.\n\nI should be able to just put the 5 minute animation on my gesture without needing a copy.\n\nAnother good example is a particular booth model from the Virtual Market 2's \"Virtual Museum B\" map. It has a gesture where the character drools and does a grabby motion with its fingers.\n\nWhile funny and unique, it causes a delay in all of the other gestures, which is lame. They could fix the delay by adding a whole copy of the avatar into the avatar... but optimally it should \"just work\".\n\nI threw 8 different idle animations onto gestures on an avatar... and I had to make 8 duplicates of my model to do it. That avatar takes a lot longer to load than if I could just animate things directly and not have 8 copies of my model.\n\nNow that disabled gameobjects are counted in performance ranking, I have the stats of having 9 models loaded at once.\n\nRelated:\nhttps://vrchat.canny.io/feature-requests/p/now-that-we-can-cancel-emotes-by-moving-let-us-use-loop-time-on-emotes\n\nhttps://vrchat.canny.io/feature-requests/p/official-way-to-loop-avatar-idle-anims",
